From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: restart the period queue at prepare

Since commit 222d04cf55bc ("ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: wrap the position of
a full ring to 0") a playback stream on SM8250 underruns: the DSP
returns each buffer as soon as it has copied it, so the position
reaches appl_ptr whenever the application has written up to a period
boundary. Before that commit the position stayed one frame short and
the underrun was never seen.

The recovery from it never plays again. ALSA stops the stream, the
application prepares it and starts it, and ALSA restarts appl_ptr from
0, but q6asm_dai_ack() keeps counting from the queue_ptr of the
previous run. appl_ptr - queue_ptr is negative, no period is queued
again, the DSP returns nothing and the stream stays RUNNING, silent,
for good. The hw pointer of the port is stale as well: it keeps the
token of the last buffer of the previous run, so the position reported
after prepare is that of the previous run, not 0.

Seen on a Mangmi Pocket Max with PipeWire: Steam's boot sound plays,
then every later sound is a single period followed by silence.

Clear queue_ptr in q6asm_dai_prepare() and reset the hw pointer where
q6asm_map_memory_regions() sets up the ring again, as commit
0337b8129cf6 ("ASoC: qcom: q6apm: reset the hw pointer with the
fragment queue") does for q6apm.

Fixes: 222d04cf55bc ("ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: wrap the position of a full ring to 0")
Signed-off-by: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c | 2 ++
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c     | 1 +
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
index 21eb758..ca582eb 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
@@ -222,6 +222,8 @@ static int q6asm_dai_prepare(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	}
 
 	prtd->pcm_count = snd_pcm_lib_period_bytes(substream);
+	/* ALSA restarts the ring from 0, so does the queue of periods */
+	prtd->queue_ptr = 0;
 	/* rate and channels are sent to audio driver */
 	if (prtd->state == Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING) {
 		/* clear the previous setup if any  */
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c
index de0bd8f..594dc5c 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c
@@ -525,6 +525,7 @@ int q6asm_map_memory_regions(unsigned int dir, struct audio_client *ac,
 		}
 	}
 	ac->port[dir].num_periods = periods;
+	atomic_set(&ac->port[dir].hw_ptr, 0);
 
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&ac->lock, flags);
 
